---
import Docs from '../../layouts/Docs.astro';
import SwitchDemo from '../../components/SwitchDemo';
import CodeBlock from '../../components/CodeBlock.astro';
---

<Docs title="Switch" description="An on/off control for settings that apply right away.">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Switch</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    A track and thumb that turns one setting on or off. Use it for settings that take effect at once, such as
    notifications or model access.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8">
    <SwitchDemo client:load />
  </div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Switch usage"
      code={`import { Switch } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/switch";
import { Label } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/label";
import { SettingsRow } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/settings-list";

const [paused, setPaused] = useState(false);

<Label>
  <Switch checked={paused} onCheckedChange={setPaused} />
  Pause motion
</Label>

<SettingsRow label="Email summaries" htmlFor="summary">
  <Switch id="summary" defaultChecked />
</SettingsRow>

<Switch
  aria-label={\`Allow \${model.name}\`}
  checked={model.enabled}
  disabled={saving}
  aria-busy={pending}
  onCheckedChange={(enabled) => save(model.id, enabled)}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      Pass <code>checked</code> and <code>onCheckedChange</code> to control the switch, or <code>defaultChecked</code>{' '}
      to let it keep its own state.
      <code>onCheckedChange</code> gets a boolean, so a state setter can be passed straight in.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Props</h2>
    <p>
      <code>size</code> is <code>"md"</code> (the default, a 32 × 18px track with a 16px thumb) or <code>"sm"</code> (a
      24 × 14px track with a 12px thumb). Both have a hit area 12px wider and 8px taller on each side.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>disabled</code> dims the switch and blocks changes; a disabled
      <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code> around it does the same. Set
      <code>aria-invalid</code> to draw a danger border and ring. Set
      <code>aria-busy</code> while a change is saving to show a progress cursor.
    </p>
    <p>
      The switch also takes Base UI props such as <code>id</code>,<code>name</code>, <code>value</code>,{' '}
      <code>required</code>,<code>readOnly</code>, <code>inputRef</code>, and state functions for
      <code>className</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      Switch renders an element with <code>role="switch"</code> and
      <code>aria-checked</code>, plus a hidden input for forms. Tab moves focus to it, and Space or Enter toggles it. A
      focused switch shows a 2px focus ring. Name every switch with a wrapping <code>Label</code>, a
      <code>Label htmlFor</code> or <code>SettingsRow htmlFor</code>, or
      <code>aria-label</code>.
    </p>
    <p>
      The track color changes in 120ms and the thumb slides in 180ms. Both stop when reduced motion is requested. The
      thumb slides the other way in right-to-left text. In forced colors mode the track gets a system border and an on
      switch is highlighted.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Theme tokens</h2>
    <p>
      Off uses a <code>--sprout-muted</code> track with a<code>--sprout-surface</code> thumb (<code>--sprout-text</code>{' '}
      in dark mode). On uses <code>--sprout-primary</code> with a<code>--sprout-on-primary</code> thumb, so the opt-in
      TulipFarm theme tints it green. Invalid uses <code>--sprout-danger</code>, and focus uses
      <code>--sprout-focus</code>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
